      "description": "JUNIOR GROUP LEADER (F/M) Genetics and Developmental Biology - UMR3215/U934 | PSL Paramètres d’accessibilité fermer Contrastes Défaut Renforcer Inverser Police (dyslexie) Défaut Adapter Interlignage Défaut Augmenter Justification Défaut Supprimer Aller au contenu principal fr ▼ fr en Menu RH Découvrir PSL Nos établissements La recherche à PSL La formation à PSL L’innovation à PSL Nos engagements La qualité au cœur de la stratégie RH Favoriser le développement des compétences Une université inclusive et sans discrimination Une université responsable et ouverte Index égalité professionnelle Formation Centre d'Innovation Pédagogique Ecole Interne Toutes nos offres Recrutement Primary tabs Voir Generate PDF JUNIOR GROUP LEADER (F/M) Genetics and Developmental Biology - UMR3215/U934 (F/H) Poste à pourvoir le  03/05/2027 Localisation du poste 75005, Paris, France Télécharger en pdf Partager : Facebook Linked in Imprimer Postuler Environnement et contexte de travail Notre établissement fait partie de l'Université PSL. Située au cœur de Paris, celle-ci fait dialoguer tous les domaines du savoir, de l'innovation et de la création. Classée parmi les 50 premières universités mondiales, elle forme au plus près de la recherche des chercheurs, artistes, ingénieurs, entrepreneurs ou dirigeants conscients de leur responsabilité sociale, individuelle et collective. Structure d'accueil Institut Curie Research Center Institut Curie , France's leading cancer center, comprises a state-of-the-art hospital specialized in cancer treatment and an internationally renowned multidisciplinary research center combining research in cell biology, genetics, epigenetics, immunology, soft matter physics, organic chemistry, and medicinal chemistry. It brings together more than 4,000 researchers, doctors, clinicians, technicians, and administrative staff across three sites: Paris, Orsay, and Saint-Cloud. The institute's facilities include an advanced imaging platform with a wide variety of high-end microscopes, from confocal to super-resolution imaging, imaging of living cells and small animals. Other facilities include single-cell technologies, small molecule and CRISPR screening, high-throughput sequencing, bioinformatics, proteomics and mass spectrometry, antibody technologies and protein purification, nano-SIMS, cytometry, and animal housing. In addition, the proximity to the hospital allows to access to large clinical databases and sample collections and an exceptional environment for pediatric oncology research. Missions Activités principales The Genetics and Developmental Biology unit (UMR3215/U934) at Institut Curie is recruiting a Junior Group Leader to develop an independent, ambitious and innovative research program that complements the unit’s scientific expertise. Research conducted within UMR3215/U934 covers a broad range of topics in developmental biology, including stem cells, tissue growth and morphogenesis, epigenetics, genomics, integrated physiology, metabolism and synthetic embryo models. Particular attention will be given to projects aimed at improving the understanding of the mechanisms underlying development, homeostasis and regeneration, using animal models, organoids or other innovative experimental approaches. The successful candidate will join a leading multidisciplinary and international scientific environment within the Institut Curie Research Center and Université PSL. They will benefit from laboratory space to host a team of 6 to 7 people, as well as a competitive start-up package including the initial salary of the Group Leader. Profil du candidat Savoirs et compétences attendus Education and knowledge Candidates must hold a PhD and have completed postdoctoral research experience. Required skills Candidates must demonstrate their ability to lead an independent, ambitious and innovative research program that fully integrates into the unit’s scientific environment. Applications are encouraged across all areas of developmental biology and related disciplines, including stem cells, tissue growth and morphogenesis, epigenetics, genomics, metabolism, integrated physiology, synthetic embryo models, as well as mechanisms of homeostasis and regeneration. Candidates will be expected to actively contribute to the unit’s collective scientific dynamics and to develop collaborations with teams at the Institut Curie Research Center. All our opportunities are open to people with disabilities. Contract information Contract type : Fixed-term contract Start date : During 2027 Duration : Up to 2 years, with the aim of securing a permanent position through CNRS, Inserm or the University Working time : Full time Salary : According to the applicable salary scales Benefits : Staff restaurant, 70% coverage of the annual public transport pass, company health insurance Location : 26 rue d’Ulm, 75005 Paris, France Contact To apply, please send a full CV, a cover letter, a brief description of past achievements (1 to 2 pages), a detailed 5-year research program (5 pages),and the email contacts of 3 referees who may be contacted: Publication date: 15 September 2026 Application deadline: 15 December 2026. Interviews are scheduled for 30 and 31 March 2027. Institut Curie is an inclusive, equal-opportunity employer. It is also committed to upholding high standards of research integrity. https://euraxess.ec.europa.eu/sites/default/files/brochures/eur_21620_en-fr.pdf Diplôme et expérience professionnelle Bac+6 et plus Non discrimination, ouverture et transparence Notre établissement, comme l'ensemble de l'Université PSL, s’engage à soutenir et promouvoir l’égalité, la diversité et l’inclusion au sein de ses communautés. Nous encourageons les candidatures issues de profils variés, que nous veillerons à sélectionner via un processus de recrutement ouvert et transparent. Contact lrg7b3lwv75k@emploi.beetween.com Autres informations Rémunération 3628.8 € (Euros) par mois Type de contrat / de poste CDD Durée du contrat 2 an(s) Quotité de travail Référence lrg7b3lwv7 Publié le 15/09/2026 Postuler JUNIOR GROUP LEADER (F/M) Genetics and Developmental Biology - UMR3215/U934 (F/H) Poste à pourvoir le  03/05/2027 Localisation du poste 75005, Paris, France Établissement Institut Curie Environnement et contexte de travail Notre établissement fait partie de l'Université PSL. Située au cœur de Paris, celle-ci fait dialoguer tous les domaines du savoir, de l'innovation et de la création. Classée parmi les 50 premières universités mondiales, elle forme au plus près de la recherche des chercheurs, artistes, ingénieurs, entrepreneurs ou dirigeants conscients de leur responsabilité sociale, individuelle et collective. Structure d'accueil Institut Curie Research Center Institut Curie , France's leading cancer center, comprises a state-of-the-art hospital specialized in cancer treatment and an internationally renowned multidisciplinary research center combining research in cell biology, genetics, epigenetics, immunology, soft matter physics, organic chemistry, and medicinal chemistry. It brings together more than 4,000 researchers, doctors, clinicians, technicians, and administrative staff across three sites: Paris, Orsay, and Saint-Cloud. The institute's facilities include an advanced imaging platform with a wide variety of high-end microscopes, from confocal to super-resolution imaging, imaging of living cells and small animals. Other facilities include single-cell technologies, small molecule and CRISPR screening, high-throughput sequencing, bioinformatics, proteomics and mass spectrometry, antibody technologies and protein purification, nano-SIMS, cytometry, and animal housing. In addition, the proximity to the hospital allows to access to large clinical databases and sample collections and an exceptional environment for pediatric oncology research. Missions Activités principales The Genetics and Developmental Biology unit (UMR3215/U934) at Institut Curie is recruiting a Junior Group Leader to develop an independent, ambitious and innovative research program that complements the unit’s scientific expertise. Research conducted within UMR3215/U934 covers a broad range of topics in developmental biology, including stem cells, tissue growth and morphogenesis, epigenetics, genomics, integrated physiology, metabolism and synthetic embryo models. Particular attention will be given to projects aimed at improving the understanding of the mechanisms underlying development, homeostasis and regeneration, using animal models, organoids or other innovative experimental approaches. The successful candidate will join a leading multidisciplinary and international scientific environment within the Institut Curie Research Center and Université PSL. They will benefit from laboratory space to host a team of 6 to 7 people, as well as a competitive start-up package including the initial salary of the Group Leader. Profil du candidat Savoirs et compétences attendus Education and knowledge Candidates must hold a PhD and have completed postdoctoral research experience. Required skills Candidates must demonstrate their ability to lead an independent, ambitious and innovative research program that fully integrates into the unit’s scientific environment. Applications are encouraged across all areas of developmental biology and related disciplines, including stem cells, tissue growth and morphogenesis, epigenetics, genomics, metabolism, integrated physiology, synthetic embryo models, as well as mechanisms of homeostasis and regeneration. Candidates will be expected to actively contribute to the unit’s collective scientific dynamics and to develop collaborations with teams at the Institut Curie Research Center. All our opportunities are open to people with disabilities. Contract information Contract type : Fixed-term contract Start date : During 2027 Duration : Up to 2 years, with the aim of securing a permanent position through CNRS, Inserm or the University Working time : F